+**Erase writer model (V1-02/V1-03, revised this branch).** The framebuffer erase
+is a *clock-counted writer*, not a pixel-counted one:
+- One 16-bit word per 8 VDP1 clocks (pinned Ymir
+  `docs/dev-notes/system-info/vdp1-erase-swap-timings.txt`); the writer never
+  stores a partial word, so the sub-word remainder is carried in
+  `vblank_erase_pool` / `m_vdp1_display_erase.pool`.
+- VBlank (VBE=1) erase: budget `vdp1_vblank_erase_capacity()` = (raster clocks
+  − 200) × blanking rasters from ST-013 Table 4.5, spent one raster quota per
+  physical raster by the scanline callback (`vdp1_advance_vblank_erase`); field
+  end charges only the final raster quota (`vdp1_finish_vblank_erase`), so
+  unspent blanking time is never retroactively written.
+- Display-period erase (manual clear/change modes): the writer follows the
+  readout of a *presented* raster and can erase only rows whose presentation
+  completed (`vdp1_advance_display_erase`), one raster clock quota per
+  completed raster, capped at `vblank_start − 2`; a row that reaches the
+  eligible-row edge cannot bank its unspent clocks.
+- Window units: EWLR/EWRR hold 8-dot coordinates (Ymir `vdp1_regs.hpp` stores
+  `eraseX1 = field << 3`), intersected with the visible dots (active + 4 dots,
+  or + 8 in the wide modes, per ST-013 printed p.49) and only then converted to
+  the 16-bit words the writer stores: 8-bit display modes pack two dots per
+  word, so both window edges divide by `dots_per_word` and the right edge rounds
+  up to cover the partial word.
+- CPU/SCU contention: an occupied framebuffer access costs the erase
+  `VDP1_CPU_ACCESS_STEAL` (13) clocks, deducted from the next raster's quota
+  (ST-013 printed p.20 priority). The deduction is observable only while a row
+  is longer than a raster's word quota; otherwise the row edge absorbs it and
+  only the pool remainder differs (both cases are covered by
+  `regtests/saturn/test_vdp1.py`).
+
