+  // into two areas is programmed with no-access or CPU read/write, that memory
+  // performs no display fetch and the CPU is granted at any timing, which is
+  // the documented way to use a VRAM bank as work RAM. A bank executing
+  // rotation accesses ignores its cycle pattern register (printed p.31), so it
+  // is never idle in this sense.
